    {
      "id": "v6/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top1/r01/G3",
      "evidence_sha256": "09fcfa4e83da7d263f34e895edaa4139fb0eadedff33172c0a96aa608aaf102b",
      "assessment": "R1 G3 correctly reads control 2 as steps 51-75 and observes the roughly 40% local increase in delivered guidance (inside RMS 8.83758e-5 to 1.23731e-4 A; max-atom mean 1.16940e-4 to 1.63735e-4 A). It excludes clipping on the observed trajectories and queries A/B contributions and fixed score quartiles. Yet it marks the expected geometric improvement refuted even though mean condition improves by 0.000146372 A, because the result is below the 0.02 A ranking tolerance. That tolerance is not measurement resolution or a no-effect threshold. It claims other windows are byte-identical, although the later 76-90 and 91-99 diagnostics differ. It also mixes legal chemical-subgraph coverage with the separate geometric Hungarian correspondence.",
      "decision_update": "The agent proposes early amplification [7,5,7,5] and late reduction [5,5,7,3], both single-control changes from its anchor. The synthesizer does not select either. Its move toward temporal propagation is useful, but its falsifiers prematurely close a direction when a small response persists. An improved generic strategy should first ask whether the intervention changed the actuator, then where its effect persists or attenuates, and whether the observed trade-off changes the next ranking decision. Small signed effects should guide a local sensitivity model even when they do not make condition priority decisive.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The correct interval mapping and direct transmission measurement are positive counterexamples to G1. It expressly keeps geometry-to-affinity coupling unresolved rather than declaring it proven. However, assertions about a Best jump implying discrete chemistry, a top-quartile response, and a local response being functionally unreachable exceed the observations; categorical or node-level evidence was not queried. The maximum individual condition delta is about 0.000656 A, not the claimed 0.00047 A.",
