    {
      "id": "v6/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top1/r01/G4",
      "evidence_sha256": "dd39ef41ca8f75ba43172a426fd9defa7f9254d35b594f83438947e18ff7c279",
      "assessment": "R1 G4 correctly distinguishes unguided 0-9 from control 0 at 10-25. The [5,5,5,3] intervention reduces late inside displacement from 1.90674e-4 to 1.14487e-4 A, with condition +0.000420280 A, affinity-gap -0.000104914 and no validity conversions. It appropriately rejects clipping as an explanation on these trajectories and looks for higher-delivery early windows. But it converts one small edge into a broad instruction to stop editing the late window. It presumes the largest baseline-error candidates must be the largest responders; actual largest condition changes include c004 and c021, not just the listed c002/c009/c016. Control-1 cosine is misquoted as 0.0017 from 10-25 instead of the 26-50 value 0.0575368.",
      "decision_update": "The unselected proposals [7,5,5,3] and [5,3,5,3] test different windows on the late-down background. They are legitimate candidates, but claims that two flat probes would close amplitude exploration or uniquely identify overwriting are too strong. A useful general improvement is to choose experiments that distinguish competing propagation mechanisms using node-level current/endpoint evidence, and separate residual-error level from intervention sensitivity before assigning diagnostic priority. The initial response used an invalid tool ID with an extra b; the repair corrected that citation and kept the scientific arrays.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "Unlike G1, G4's boundary mapping is correct and its description of delivered control changing is supported. Its bracket proposals are not scientific failures merely because they were unselected. The evidence supports non-clipping only for observed paths, not every possible future amplitude. Missing chemical-pose mappings in 20/25 candidates cannot establish that chemistry causes the affinity gap, and the assertion that only Best matters if Mean is insensitive conflicts with the functional objective.",
